    <innerclass refid="classterminal_1_1_link_detector" prot="public">terminal::LinkDetector</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceterminal">terminal</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Pure string utility for classifying terminal tokens as file paths or URLs. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>LinkDetector is a stateless header-only utility with no dependencies on the terminal grid, screen state, or any JUCE component. It provides:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>A built-in set of known file extensions (populated once via a static local).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Extension extraction and case-insensitive lookup.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classURL" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/doxygen/doc/juce.tag">URL</ref> protocol prefix detection.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>A unified <computeroutput>classify()</computeroutput> entry point returning a <computeroutput>LinkType</computeroutput> enum.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Config-driven extension merging (user extensions from end.lua) is intentionally left to the caller — this class knows nothing about Config.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>All methods are <computeroutput>noexcept</computeroutput>. No dynamic allocation occurs on the hot path after the built-in set is first constructed. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
